 35S     36S(P,D)                      2026JO01                  ENSDF    202509
 35S   H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2025$          
 35S  c  J|p=0+ for {+36}S g.s.                                                 
 35S  c  2026Jo01: A 66-MeV dispersion-matched proton beam was produced from the
 35S 2c  Separated Sector Cyclotron facility of iThemba LABS, South Africa. The 
 35S 3c  target was 1-mg/cm{+2}, 99.24%-enriched {+36}S powder encapsulated     
 35S 4c  between two 0.5-|mm Mylar foils. The outgoing deuteron and triton      
 35S 5c  reaction products momentum-analyzed by the K=600                       
 35S 6c  quadrupole-dipole-dipole magnetic spectrometer and detected by the     
 35S 7c  focal-plane detectors consisting of two multiwire drift chambers (MWDC)
 35S 8c  and a downstream plastic scintillator. Measured |s(E{-d},|q). Deduced  
 35S 9c  98 levels, L-transfers and single-neutron spectroscopic factors for 81 
 35S Ac  levels from zero-range adiabatic distorted-wave approximation (ADWA)   
 35S Bc  calculations using DWUCK4. Deduced J-dependence of L=2 angular         
 35S Cc  distributions and reproduced with finite-range ADWA calculations.      
 35S Dc  Comparisons with large-scale shell-model and ab initio calculations.   
 35S Ec  Confirmed the N=20 shell closure in {+36}S.                            
 35S  cL J,L,S$From ADWA analysis of the measured |s(|q) in 2026Jo01, unless    
 35S 2cL otherwise noted.                                                       
